  node_types RepositoryOwner
  node_types PhysicalRoot
  edge_types physically_owned_by
  invariant an organ builds on every environment it is expected to run in: a POSIX feature pin that hides the BSD interfaces a file already uses makes it uncompilable on the control plane while still building on the deploy host, so the pin carries a platform guard rather than a silent per-machine capability difference
  invariant a WAL-mode store is copied through a consistent snapshot, never by copying the main database file alone: the write-ahead log routinely holds more recent state than the file beside it, so a plain cp yields a backup that restores silently to an older moment and reports no error while doing it
  invariant a tenant never appears in the name of an organ's functions, environment variables or routes: a delegated vertical is resolved from the namespace contract, so a second vertical needs a contract row rather than a parallel accessor, route and variable for every one of its parts; table names still carrying a tenant are a schema migration and are named here as owed rather than treated as done
  invariant an institutional fact is declared once and rendered, never asserted independently by each organ that needs it: the settlement rail, the estate list, the served carriers and the content-type set each have a contract in architecture/ and a generator or checker, so a fact asserted in four places cannot drift into four different answers with nothing to notice
  invariant a store is named by a declaration and never by the caller's working directory: an organ resolves an explicit flag, then the environment's declaration, then one machine store under the state root, and refuses while naming the variable to set rather than creating a store beside $PWD; a bare-filename default produces stores that are indistinguishable from the real one once they exist
  invariant a delegating organ resolves a peer organ in both shipped layouts: an explicit environment override first, then a peer in the same directory as the running binary (the managed install, where every organ is a peer in one bin directory), then the checkout sibling under its own component directory, each confirmed by a real executable test; resolving only the checkout shape breaks delegation in every installation the software actually ships as
  invariant campaigns and runs are evidence, fixtures, packs, receipts, or operator state rather than parallel implementation roots
  invariant independently buildable product components live under components and the notebook-era 10-Code root cannot return
  invariant any root consumed by a background carrier must physically reside outside macOS TCC-protected Desktop/Documents/Downloads territory; a compatibility path may be a symlink, but its resolved root must be readable by the carrier
  invariant retired notebook writers live under evidence origins and cannot remain scheduled production services
  invariant the legacy estate compiler remains retired unless a successor names a current Atlas architecture and owner, uses a non-append-only snapshot state model, and declares positive age, byte, and snapshot-count retention bounds
  forbidden_inference physical placement -> semantic authority
  forbidden_inference a configured BONFYRE_ROOT path -> that a background process may read it
  forbidden_inference a documented YaFF Scan design -> authority to run an estate compiler
  source_lineage Generation-10 repository convergence
  witness 2026-08-30 LaunchAgent-backed MCP used the Developer root directly while the legacy Documents compatibility symlink remained valid; local Atlas/status/tree and Oracle-tunneled Atlas reads passed
